gifts along the way. Despite Tanzler's efforts,&nbsp;
she died. However, Tanzler's obsession with Dear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:06.600
Maria would not stop at her death. He paid for&nbsp;
her burial in a pricey mausoleum and visited her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:11.100
there almost every night for two years. That was&nbsp;
until he lost his job, probably for being too much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:15.780
of a simp. He crept into the cemetery one night&nbsp;
in 1933, removed her body from the mausoleum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.800
and took her to an old hollowed-out airplane,&nbsp;
where he used DIY techniques to preserve her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

