However, a gunshot wound is no match for Sartain's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.960
obsession. After a few hours in hospital care,&nbsp;
which happens to be just long enough for Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.500
to begin his rampage through Haddonfield,&nbsp;
Sartain catches up with Deputy Hawkins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:08.760
where he meets Laurie Strode and, for&nbsp;
lack of a better term, goes full fangirl.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:10.571
- Laurie Strode.

00:09:10.571 --> 00:09:12.811
- [Sheriff Barker] Laurie Strode, meet Dr. Sartain.

00:09:12.811 --> 00:09:16.383
- I read everything about&nbsp;
you and Michael. Everything.

00:09:16.383 --> 00:09:19.740
- Dr. Sartain expresses this extreme&nbsp;
fascination with Laurie because she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:23.160
one of the few people alive who has&nbsp;
seen Michael killing in the wild, which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:27.120
as I mentioned earlier, he's very jealous&nbsp;
of. The other survivors are either too young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:31.440
or they just didn't see very much of him. Being&nbsp;
that Sartain is most familiar with his patient,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:35.100
Hawkins brings him along to help with&nbsp;
the search. It's here that he exposes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:39.000
his own obsessive doctor disorder through the&nbsp;
excitement evident when talking about Michael.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:44.400
- [Sartain] I want to know what he's feeling. I want&nbsp;
to know what pleasure he gets out of killing.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:49.020
- He even warns Hawkins that Michael is considered&nbsp;
property of the state and must not be harmed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:52.500
further solidifying that his motivations&nbsp;
for studying Michael are far different than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:56.820
Dr. Loomis's. Loomis is what fans of true&nbsp;
crime would refer to as being pro-victim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:01.080
whereas Dr. Sartain wouldn't feel out&nbsp;
of place browsing serial killer merch on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:04.860
Etsy. In the original "Halloween," Loomis was&nbsp;
armed with a gun, so he believed that he didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:08.400
have much to fear when going after Michael.&nbsp;
In Sartain's case, he has a different reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:12.540
to believe that he's not in danger. Often, when&nbsp;
serial killers go to prison, they get letters from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:16.740
people who are essentially fans that desire to be&nbsp;
close to them. According to some experts, these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:20.820
fans have a sexual attraction, while others don't&nbsp;
believe that it necessarily has to be. According&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:25.020
