to psychopathically obsessed. He has a hidden&nbsp;
scalpel blade inside his pen, so he does his best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:01.800
Ezio Auditore on Officer Hawkins, dropping him to&nbsp;
the ground. Up until this point, he had expressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:06.468
several times that he really wanted to know what&nbsp;
Michael felt like while killing, so he exclaims-

00:12:06.468 --> 00:12:08.880
- [Sartain] So this is what it feels like.

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:12.420
- which solidifies the idea that if&nbsp;
he ever wanted to solve the mystery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:16.800
of Michael Myers for scientific purposes to&nbsp;
better humanity, that is no longer the case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:21.000
because it doesn't make sense to become a&nbsp;
killer in order to try to stop one. Then again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:24.540
there are people who spend thousands of dollars&nbsp;
on credit cards so they can save a couple bucks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:28.980
on airline miles. I just don't take Sartain&nbsp;
to be that much of an idiot. I think he knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:33.300
Michael won't be free forever and he's desperate&nbsp;
to learn as much as he can about him for purely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:37.920
selfish reasons. It's like I said earlier: he&nbsp;
likes to feel important. And it doesn't stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:42.360
there. Sartain puts on Michael's mask and stares&nbsp;
at a terrified Allyson through the car window,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:46.800
just to, as he put it himself, see what it&nbsp;
feels like. After loading Michael into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:50.820
back of the locked police car where Allyson is&nbsp;
now trapped, he drives away over Hawkins' body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:55.620
and tells Allyson that he is bringing Michael to&nbsp;
Laurie Strode to set up a reunion. His theory is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:59.580
that Michael stays alive to continue hunting&nbsp;
Laurie and that Laurie stays alive to continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:04.200
fighting Michael. He also tells Allyson how badly&nbsp;
he wants to hear Michael speak. He is convinced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:08.760
that only Laurie Strode can bring this out of him.&nbsp;
Off of this information, Allyson devises a plan on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:12.480
the spot to try to free herself from the back of&nbsp;
the car. She claims that she had heard Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:16.860
speak when he killed her friend and offers him&nbsp;
a deal. If Sartain lets her out, she'll tell him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:20.940
what Michael said. However, Sartain's excitement&nbsp;
over the possibility over what Michael could've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:25.020
said completely distracts him. He guesses at&nbsp;
what the supposed spoken word might've been,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:28.920
like an excited parent who just found out their&nbsp;
kid spoke his first word from the babysitter.

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:32.819
- What was the word? Was it&nbsp;
the sister's name? Judith?

00:13:32.819 --> 00:13:37.380
- But before getting his answer, Michael wakes&nbsp;
up and swiftly kicks in Dr. Sartain's seat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:41.760
then proceeds to drag the injured psychologist&nbsp;
out of the car. His final moments are the perfect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:46.620
microcosm for his entire character, because&nbsp;
instead of pleading for his life or showing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:51.180
any kind of fear at all, he's completely focused&nbsp;
on asking Michael to say something. Right until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:56.940
the end, his actions are dictated by his ODD, his&nbsp;
obsession to understand his patient. Ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.940 --> 00:14:01.320
he does not get into Michael's head,&nbsp;
but Michael's foot gets into his.&nbsp;&nbsp;

